<div class="cvp-wizard-body">

  <div class="cvp-wizard-progress">Step {{stepNumber}} of {{totalSteps}}</div>

  {{#if isPitch}}
  <div class="cvp-wizard-step cvp-wizard-pitch">
    <h2>Make Your Campaign Portable</h2>
    <p>
      Right now, your campaign lives entirely inside this one World — every scene, actor, item, and
      journal entry, tangled together with everything else on this install. That's fine, until the day
      it isn't:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your computer dies, or you switch machines.</li>
      <li>You want to run this campaign for a different group, or hand it to a co-GM.</li>
      <li>You want to back it up somewhere that isn't "hope this World never corrupts."</li>
      <li>You want to share it — with your table, or with the world.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Packaging it as a real, standalone Foundry module — the same kind of thing you'd install from
      the package browser — solves all of that at once. It takes some effort up front. But that effort
      is <strong>small and constant</strong> if you do it now, and it only grows the longer you wait:
      every session adds more content that isn't packaged yet, more that would need to be found,
      checked, and pulled in later. A campaign packaged from day one costs you an afternoon. The same
      campaign packaged after two years of play can cost you a week — if you can even reconstruct it
      accurately at all.
    </p>
    <p>
      This wizard won't do it all invisibly — there's one step near the end where Foundry itself
      requires you to visit the Setup screen, since a running World can't install a new package into
      itself. But everything else, including figuring out <em>what</em> belongs in the package, is
      handled here.
    </p>
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  {{#if isSelect}}
  <div class="cvp-wizard-step cvp-wizard-select">
    <h2>What belongs in this campaign?</h2>
    <p>
      This step checks whether you have <strong>Tagger</strong> installed — a free, separate
      <em>add-on module</em>, not something built into Foundry itself. Like any module, it has to be
      installed and enabled on its own (from the Add-on Modules tab on Foundry's Setup screen) before
      it does anything. If it's there and active, this wizard reads the tags you've already applied
      to your scenes, actors, items, and journals with it, and uses them to guess what belongs to this
      campaign — so you don't have to pick everything by hand in the next step. If it's not installed,
      that's completely fine; it's an optional shortcut, not a requirement, and you'll just do that
      picking by hand instead.
    </p>

    {{#if taggerActive}}
      {{#if hasTagGroups}}
      <p>
        Tagger is installed and active, and it already found tags applied in this World. Pick the tag
        (or tags) below that represent this campaign — everything carrying them becomes the starting
        point for the Adventure in the next step. You'll still be able to add or remove individual
        pieces there by hand.
      </p>
      <div class="cvp-wizard-tag-list">
        {{#each tagGroups as |group|}}
        <label class="cvp-wizard-tag-row">
          <input type="checkbox" name="campaignTag" value="{{group.tag}}" {{#if group.selected}}checked{{/if}}>
          <span class="cvp-wizard-tag-name">{{group.tag}}</span>
          <span class="cvp-wizard-tag-summary">{{group.summary}}</span>
        </label>
        {{/each}}
      </div>
      <p class="cvp-wizard-hint">{{selectedCount}} tag(s) selected. Leave everything unchecked to skip straight to manual selection.</p>
      {{else}}
      <p>
        Tagger is installed and active, but nothing in this World has been tagged yet — so there's
        nothing for it to hand this wizard automatically. That's fine: you'll pick content by hand in
        the next step instead. (Tagging things with Tagger first, then re-running this wizard, makes
        future updates to this module faster — but it's entirely optional.)
      </p>
      {{/if}}
    {{else}}
    <p>
      Tagger isn't installed (or isn't enabled) in this World right now, so there's nothing for this
      wizard to read automatically — you'll pick everything by hand in the next step instead, which
      works just as well. If you'd like this step to do the grouping for you next time, install
      <strong>Tagger</strong> from the Add-on Modules tab on Foundry's Setup screen, enable it for this
      World, tag your content with it, and re-run this wizard.
    </p>
    {{/if}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  {{#if isAdventure}}
  <div class="cvp-wizard-step cvp-wizard-adventure">
    <h2>Build the Adventure</h2>
    <p>
      This is where your campaign actually becomes something packageable — a real Foundry
      <strong>Adventure</strong> document that holds the content. Nothing gets bundled unless you
      create it here, and even after you do, nothing is added to it automatically unless you selected
      tags in the previous step.
    </p>
    <div class="form-group">
      <label>Campaign name</label>
      <input type="text" class="cvp-wizard-campaign-name" value="{{campaignName}}">
    </div>

    {{#unless hasAdventure}}
    <p class="cvp-wizard-hint">{{matchPreview}}</p>
    <button type="button" data-action="createAdventure" class="cvp-wizard-btn cvp-wizard-btn--primary" {{#if creatingAdventure}}disabled{{/if}}>
      {{#if creatingAdventure}}Creating…{{else}}Create Adventure{{/if}}
    </button>
    <p class="cvp-wizard-hint">Clicking Next without doing this skips the step — you'll be asked to confirm first.</p>
    {{else}}
    <p>
      <strong>"{{adventureName}}"</strong> created — {{adventureSummary}}. Foundry's own Adventure
      Builder opened in a separate window, on its <strong>Contents</strong> tab.
    </p>
    <p>
      That tab works by <strong>drag and drop</strong> — there's no "add" button to click. Open your
      World's sidebar tabs (Actors, Items, Scenes, Journal Entries, Roll Tables, Macros, Cards, and
      Playlists) one at a time, and drag each entry you want in this campaign onto the Contents tab.
      Go through everything you want this campaign to include: every actor (PCs and the important
      NPCs/monsters), item, scene or map, journal entry (including handouts and lore), roll table,
      macro, card deck, and playlist. If you selected tags in the last step, those matches were already
      dragged in for you — it's still worth checking the Contents tab and adding anything that got
      missed, or that you never tagged.
    </p>
    <p>
      Take your time here — this is the step that decides what actually ships. You can close this
      wizard, work in the Builder for as long as you need, and come back later; nothing is lost. Use
      the button below to reopen the Builder if you've closed it.
    </p>
    <button type="button" data-action="reopenBuilder" class="cvp-wizard-btn">Reopen Builder</button>
    {{/unless}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  {{#if isModule}}
  <div class="cvp-wizard-step cvp-wizard-module">
    <h2>Generate the module</h2>

    {{#unless hasAdventure}}
    <p>Go back and create the Adventure in the previous step first — there's nothing to package yet.</p>
    {{else}}
    <div class="form-group">
      <label>Module id</label>
      <input type="text" class="cvp-wizard-module-id" value="{{moduleId}}">
      <p class="cvp-wizard-hint">Lowercase, hyphenated, no spaces — this becomes the module's folder name.</p>
    </div>
    <p>
      This is the <code>module.json</code> for a standalone module wrapping "{{adventureName}}". Copy or
      download it now — the next step covers exactly where it (and the Adventure pack's data) need to go.
    </p>
    <pre class="cvp-wizard-manifest-preview">{{manifestText}}</pre>
    <div class="cvp-wizard-manifest-actions">
      <button type="button" data-action="copyManifest" class="cvp-wizard-btn">Copy</button>
      <button type="button" data-action="downloadManifest" class="cvp-wizard-btn">Download module.json</button>
    </div>
    {{/unless}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  {{#if isHandoff}}
  <div class="cvp-wizard-step cvp-wizard-handoff">
    <h2>Finish it on the Setup screen</h2>

    {{#unless hasAdventure}}
    <p>Go back and create the Adventure first — there's nothing to hand off yet.</p>
    {{else}}

    {{#if moduleActive}}
    <p class="cvp-wizard-success">
      🎉 <strong>{{campaignName}}</strong> is live as its own module (<code>{{moduleId}}</code>) —
      Foundry already sees it as active for this World. You're done.
    </p>
    <button type="button" data-action="finish" class="cvp-wizard-btn cvp-wizard-btn--primary">Finish</button>
    {{else}}

    <p>
      Two things need to happen. The wizard can do the first one for you; the second genuinely has to
      happen outside Foundry, on disk.
    </p>

    <div class="cvp-wizard-handoff-task">
      <h3>1. The module folder itself</h3>
      {{#if moduleFolderReady}}
      <p class="cvp-wizard-hint">✓ <code>{{targetModulePath}}/module.json</code> already exists.</p>
      {{else}}
      <p>Creates <code>{{targetModulePath}}/</code> and writes <code>module.json</code> into it — the
        same content from the last step.</p>
      {{/if}}
      <button type="button" data-action="setupModuleFolder" class="cvp-wizard-btn" {{#if settingUpModule}}disabled{{/if}}>
        {{#if settingUpModule}}Working…{{else}}{{#if moduleFolderReady}}Refresh module.json{{else}}Set up the module folder{{/if}}{{/if}}
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="cvp-wizard-handoff-task">
      <h3>2. The Adventure's data (can't be done from in here)</h3>
      <p>
        Using your OS file browser — not Foundry — copy the <strong>entire folder</strong>, every file
        in it, including the ones without a file extension:
      </p>
      <pre class="cvp-wizard-path">{{packDiskPath}}</pre>
      <p>into:</p>
      <pre class="cvp-wizard-path">{{targetPackPath}}</pre>
      <p class="cvp-wizard-hint">Best done when nobody has the Adventure Builder open for it.</p>
      <label class="cvp-wizard-confirm-row">
        <input type="checkbox" class="cvp-wizard-pack-copy-confirmed" {{#if packCopyConfirmed}}checked{{/if}}>
        I've copied it.
      </label>
    </div>

    <div class="cvp-wizard-handoff-task">
      <h3>3. Tell Foundry about it</h3>
      <p>
        Open the <strong>Settings</strong> tab in the sidebar and click <strong>Return to Setup</strong>.
        In Module Management, find "{{campaignName}}", enable it for this World, then relaunch. Come
        back to this wizard afterward — it'll recognize the module is active.
      </p>
    </div>

    <button type="button" data-action="recheckStatus" class="cvp-wizard-btn">Check again</button>
    {{/if}}
    {{/unless}}
  </div>
  {{/if}}

  <div class="cvp-wizard-nav">
    {{#if canBack}}
    <button type="button" data-action="back" class="cvp-wizard-btn">Back</button>
    {{/if}}
    {{#unless isHandoff}}
    <button type="button" data-action="next" class="cvp-wizard-btn cvp-wizard-btn--primary">
      {{#if isPitch}}Get Started{{else}}Next{{/if}}
    </button>
    {{/unless}}
  </div>

</div>
